```
import React, { useState } from 'react';
import './App.css';

function App() {
  const [todos, setTodos] = useState([
    { id: 1, name: 'Buy milk', completed: false },
    { id: 2, name: 'Walk the dog', completed: false },
    { id: 3, name: 'Do laundry', completed: false }
  ]);

  const [newTodo, setNewTodo] = useState('');

  const handleSubmit = (event) => {
    event.preventDefault();
    setTodos([...todos, { id: todos.length + 1, name: newTodo, completed: false }]);
    setNewTodo('');
  };

  const toggleCompleted = (id) => {
    setTodos(
      todos.map((todo) => {
        if (todo.id === id) {
          return { ...todo, completed: !todo.completed };
        }
        return todo;
      })
    );
  };

  const deleteTodo = (id) => {
    setTodos(todos.filter((todo) => todo.id !== id));
  };

  return (
    <div className="App">
      <h1>Todo List</h1>
      <form onSubmit={handleSubmit}>
        <input
          type="text"
          value={newTodo}
          onChange={(event) => setNewTodo(event.target.value)}
          placeholder="Add new todo"
        />
        <button type="submit">Add</button>
      </form>
      <ul>
        {todos.map((todo) => (
          <li key={todo.id}>
            <input
              type="checkbox"
              checked={todo.completed}
              onChange={() => toggleCompleted(todo.id)}
            />
            <span
              style={{
                textDecoration: todo.completed ? 'line-through' : 'none'
              }}
            >
              {todo.name}
            </span>
            <button onClick={() => deleteTodo(todo.id)}>Delete</button>
          </li>
        ))}
      </ul>
    </div>
  );
}

export default App;
```
This code uses the `useState` hook to store the todo list in the component's state. The `todos` state is initialized with an array of three todo objects. The `newTodo` state is initialized with an empty string.

The `handleSubmit` function is called when the user submits the form. It adds a new todo item to the list and resets the `newTodo` input field to an empty string.

The `toggleCompleted` function is called when the user checks or unchecks a todo item. It updates the `completed` property of the corresponding todo item in the list.

The `deleteTodo` function is called when the user clicks the "Delete" button next to a todo item. It removes the corresponding todo item from the list.

The JSX component renders a form with an input field and a button to add new todo items. It also renders an unordered list of todo items, with each item containing a checkbox, a label, and a button to delete the item.

